.TH RECOVERY_RECONNECT_TOP 4 2026-05-30 Lustre "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
recovery_reconnect_top \- slowest clients in the current recovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param mdt." TARGET ".recovery_reconnect_top"
.SY
.BI "lctl get_param obdfilter." TARGET ".recovery_reconnect_top"
.SY
.BI "lctl set_param mdt." TARGET ".recovery_reconnect_top=clear"
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per MDT or OST target device
.TP
.B Config
.br
Always present
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B recovery_reconnect_top
parameter reports the
.B N
filesystem clients that took the longest to reconnect to this target
during the current recovery window, sorted descending by delay. Output
is a YAML
.B client_reconnect_top
list whose entries each report a client
.RB ( nid )
and its reconnect
.RB ( delay_sec )
in seconds. The depth
.B N
is set by the module parameter
.BR recovery_reconnect_top_n " (default 10, max 64)."
The list is reset when recovery begins, and writing any value clears it.
.PP
This is the bounded-cardinality companion to
.BR recovery_reconnect_histogram (4):
the histogram tells you the per-target distribution, this file tells
you which specific clients drove the tail.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B mdt.*.recovery_reconnect_top
.B obdfilter.*.recovery_reconnect_top
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Show the slowest clients on an MDT after a recovery:
.EX
.RB mds# " lctl get_param mdt.lfs-MDT0000.recovery_reconnect_top"
client_reconnect_top:
- { nid:   "192.168.101.7@tcp101", delay_sec:  47 }
- { nid:   "192.168.102.4@tcp102", delay_sec:   8 }
- { nid:   "192.168.102.3@tcp102", delay_sec:   7 }
- { nid:   "192.168.101.2@tcp101", delay_sec:   4 }
- { nid:   "192.168.102.5@tcp102", delay_sec:   3 }
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
.B recovery_reconnect_top
is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.18.0.
.\" commit v2_17_53
